  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "In a close-packed body-centred cubic lattice of potassium, the correct relation between the atomic radius $(r)$ of potassium and the edge-length  of the cube is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TL2Kq",
      "text": "$r=\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pW3EC",
      "text": "$r=\\frac{a}{\\sqrt{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "x86so",
      "text": "$r=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} a$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hAi9c",
      "text": "$r=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} a$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because$ For be packing, $\\sqrt{3} a=4 r \\therefore r=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\cdot a$\r\nwhere $a=$ edge length $r=$ radius of lattice sphere",
    "image": null
  },
